## Implementation

- `godot/src/ui/screens/ModesScreen.tscn` — named nodes only, no literals: header (BackButton,
  TitleLabel, SubLabel), `ModeGrid` (3 columns, 20 px gap), `SetupArea/MatchSetup` with the two
  `.setup-group`s (label + `SegmentedContainer` panel + grid; difficulty 4 columns, length 3).
- `godot/src/ui/screens/ModesScreen.gd` — cards built in code from `UiData.mode_rows()`; art
  `TextureRect` (STRETCH_KEEP_ASPECT_COVERED) in a `Panel` whose bottom border is the accent
  (career = the documented cyan fallback); card frame = the theme's own `PanelDark` /
  `PanelCardHover` boxes with the body padding moved into a `MarginContainer` (the reference's
  `-18px` art bleed); tags/fixture as data-driven bindings re-made per refresh; difficulty and
  length segmenteds built from the gate's keys; `Config.tier_index` + `prefs` for difficulty,
  `ModesSave.save_pref(…, "matchLength", …)` for length; `select_mode()` = pending mode +
  `prefs.mode` + tournament round reset + route to `characters` (`js/ui.js:1720-1729`); a locked
  card has no activation path at all (nothing is wired), exactly like the reference's
  `.mode-card:not(.mode-card--locked)` selector.
- `godot/tests/ui/screen_modes_audit.gd` + `.tscn` — 118 checks full / 123 demo.
- `.uid` sidecars for the two new `.gd` files (`uid://kuifuwjwon4ww`, `uid://pv8fql1rm29c9`).

