## Theme requests (recorded, not edited — the theme is another lane's file)

1. `SegmentedContainer` is declared on **BaseType `Panel`** (theme README §4), which a
   `PanelContainer` cannot carry. This screen reads the box out of the theme
   (`_theme_box("SegmentedContainer")`) instead of re-creating values; a
   `SegmentedCard`-style `PanelContainer` variation (or the theme owner blessing that idiom) would
   remove the workaround.
2. No variation exists for `.match-setup .setup-group` (fill `rgba(11,36,68,0.9)`, border
   `rgba(0,229,255,0.22)`, radius 14, padding 15/17/17/17): composed here from `Palette`, requested
   as `SetupGroup`.
3. The card art's own background (`#09142e` in the reference's `.mode-card__art`) is **not** a theme
   token. The art box is drawn with no fill (artwork covers it; a missing asset leaves the card's
   panel fill visible) rather than inventing a colour. Requested as a token if GATE-A wants the
   exact fill on a failed asset load.
4. The fixture line takes `Palette.fixture` through a `font_color` override on the `LabelSmall`
   variation (the variant table has no small/fixture combination); a `Fixture` variation would fold
   it in.

